    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0580" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.796/125b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-08">December 8, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>546. Please deliver paraphrase of following to Mr. H. D. Hump-stone, West India
                    Oil Company, Santiago: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“We have been instructed by the State Department to cease immediately all
                            deliveries of gasoline and oil to Syndicate Condor in Chile. The Chilean
                            Government has been notified of this step by the Embassy. You are
                            instructed to comply at once and notify customer the action you are
                            taking is based on instructions issued by the Government of the United
                            States. Signed G. H. Michler.”<anchor n="42" xml:id="d588-f1"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d588-f1" n="42" xml:id="d588-f1-content">
